# m.mjs has begun and not finished while n.mjs runs, which shows the exports of m.mjs through `export *`: C is in its dead zone. The run time serves the read under a computed name by the record of the export:
# it takes what the variable holds for the value of the binding. So the variable of an export is not born standing for its class: it is stored where the class is written.
# That no read comes in front of the store is Link's word on compiled reads alone.
# RUN(VARIABLES): plan variables mechanisms=all
# VARIABLES: variable g1 Statics JSValue Plain
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell
# SHELL: C: dead zone
# SHELL-NEXT: main: function
# RUN(CLOSED): run-in-shell mechanisms=none
# CLOSED: C: dead zone
# CLOSED-NEXT: main: function
